+## FINDINGS
+- [S3] Makefile:64 — `TEST_FULL_CLASSES_RELEASE` defined but never referenced (test-full expands `$(TEST_FULL_CLASSES_$(_ARCH)_release)` directly).
+  WHY: Dead variable risks future readers wiring the wrong list into a new target.
+- [S3] test-history.txt:249-271 — several x86_64 release census rows record `PASSED: 0 FAILED: 0` (zero TF_RELEASE tests), so the 24/24 gate passes vacuously for those classes.
+  WHY: Rows are honestly recorded (not inflated) and TF_RELEASE marking is pre-existing test design outside this patch, but gate strength for those classes depends on future test-marking, not on this wiring.
+
+## CHECK DISPOSITIONS
+1. Makefile syntax/logic: `make -pn` and `make -n test-full` parse clean; nested `$(TEST_FULL_CLASSES_$(_ARCH)_release)` resolves correctly (x86_64 release 24 tokens, aarch64 release empty → loud error as intended); token counts verified 26/24/11/8 against the B1 rows; x86_64 debug list is token-identical to the script control list; x86 debug/release codegen paths unchanged (x86 release still via `$(MAKE) release`, debug via `$(MAKE) debug`).
+2. release-elf -j safety: `$(KERNEL): $(TEST_REGISTRY_GEN)` edge exists (Makefile:506), so the single-sub-make `$(KERNEL) $(TEST_REGISTRY_GEN)` step is DAG-serialized; only the stamp-clean side effect needed isolation into its own recursive step — done. Riscv BIN separated (`KERNEL_RISCV_RELEASE_BIN`, rule 416 `KERNEL_RISCV_BIN` untouched, no alias).
+3. Selftest if/else: x86 `safe` mapping preserved byte-equivalent (`_class_file=safe` then unconditional write); non-x86 writes `$(SELFTEST_CLASSES)` and skips the second write — correct.
+4. QEMU subst: riscv `QEMU_FLAGS` references only `$(KERNEL_RISCV_BIN)` (Makefile:423), so the outer subst hits and the inner `KERNEL_DEBUG` to `KERNEL` subst is a harmless no-op; aarch64 subst unchanged.
+5. Baked-config assertion: placed in the `CLASS=none` branch after the build (only branch with an x86_64 prebuilt fast-path); the normal-class branch rebuilds release-elf fresh after writing test-config.txt, so stamp==CLASS by construction — no gap.
+6. Script: `NEXIOS_TEST_CLASSES` consumption guarded with `:-` under `set -u`; riscv override correctly skipped when the Makefile passes a list; `ARCH` always set before SUMMARY; `X86_ONLY`/`DEBUG_ONLY` skip loops intact; per-class row format untouched, SUMMARY gains `ARCH=` tag only.
+7. strncpy gate: open/close `#if` symmetric, comment matches the widened condition, x86_64 still excluded, block is top-level (prior riscv64 block closed above).
+8. serial_input guard: declaration `CONFIG_DEBUG && CONFIG_ARCH_RISCV64` exactly matches both use sites (`loopback_begin` else-branch active iff DEBUG&&RISCV64; `loopback_end` same guard) — release TU has no dangling reference.
+9. History rows: aarch64 22 rows → 10 clean + testrunner (expected-panic) + task_fpu (empty) = 12 ok, 10 fail matching the 10 documented exclusions; x86 release 24 rows all `FAILED: 0` matching the 24-token list; riscv extension counts 5/11/13/19/5/7 plus hal 56/1 and ui 20/34 match the claimed census.
+10. Deviations: (i) LTO double-stamp skipped — reasonable, `check-release-stamp` still runs as step 1 and LTO_STAMP is a debug-mode tracker; (ii) vendored picolibc `-j` race — pre-existing, serial-make green, correctly left out of scope.
+
+DECISION: APPROVED
